& [ActivationIdentity] is the bounded Phase 1 implementation authority
  + [canonical_specification_uuid] is 50f6f41c-f35b-4844-93cb-38593db6acc0
  + [profile] is cantor-supervised-mock-loop/0.1
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [implementation_unit] is a safe Rust cantor_ecosystem library crate
  + [status] is authorized_for_phase_1_only
  + [semantic_authority] remains in caller-supplied cantor_core protocol execution
  + [agent_authority] is one deterministic commissioned mock cycle
  + [effect_authority] is none

& [AuthorityGrant] is the commission and work-packet capability set
  + [projects] is a closed set of project identifiers
  + [semantic_operations] is a closed set of Cantor operations
  + [tool_capabilities] is a closed set of tool classes
  + [data_scopes] is a closed set of readable or writable data boundaries
  + [effect_classes] is a closed set of exterior action classes
  = must: define subset containment and intersection deterministically
  = must: reject any work packet or message authority not contained by the active commission
  - never: infer effect authority from semantic, tool, project, or data authority

& [CommissionContract] is the root agency boundary
  + [profile] is cantor-commission/0.1
  + [commission_uuid] is immutable identity and the cycle correlation root
  + [principal] is one exact ParticipantAddress
  + [manager] is one exact ParticipantAddress
  + [purpose] is non-empty bounded text
  + [requested_result] is non-empty bounded text
  + [authority_grant] is AuthorityGrant
  + [required_review_checks] includes honesty, security, protocol, acceptance_criteria, and effect_boundary
  + [evidence_obligation] is a non-empty closed identifier set
  + [proof_obligation] is a non-empty closed identifier set
  + [budget] is maximum messages, serialized bytes, call depth, and logical ticks
  + [activated_at_tick] is deterministic logical time
  + [expires_at_tick] is greater than activated_at_tick
  + [lifecycle] is active, revoked, expired, completed, or faulted
  = must: validate identity, role, text, obligations, budget, lifetime, and active lifecycle before assignment
  - never: let the manager issue, widen, reactivate, or extend its own commission

& [WorkPacket] is one bounded assignment
  + [profile] is cantor-work-packet/0.1
  + [work_packet_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [commission_uuid] is the governing commission
  + [worker] is one exact CodexThread address
  + [Cantor_participant] is one exact CantorParticipant address
  + [Observer] is one exact Observer address
  + [subject] is non-empty bounded semantic focus
  + [purpose] is non-empty bounded assignment purpose
  + [requested_result] is non-empty bounded result contract
  + [acceptance_criteria] is a non-empty set of stable identifiers and descriptions
  + [authority_grant] is a subset of CommissionContract authority
  + [frame_digest] is a valid SHA-256 ContentDigest
  + [budget] is no broader than the commission budget
  = must: validate before the assignment envelope is admitted

| [ParticipantRole] is (principal | manager | codex_thread | cantor_participant | observer | effect_broker)

& [ParticipantAddress] is exact role plus stable SemanticId
  + [role] is one ParticipantRole
  + [identity] is a validated SemanticId
  = must: compare role and identity together
  - never: route by role alone when more than one identity can exist

| [MessageKind] is (commission | assignment | cantor_query | cantor_return | candidate | review | decision | fault)

& [EcosystemMessageEnvelope] is the shared message contract
  + [profile] is cantor-ecosystem-message/0.1
  + [message_uuid] is immutable SemanticId
  + [causation_uuid] is absent only for the root commission message
  + [correlation_uuid] is the active commission_uuid
  + [sender] is one exact ParticipantAddress
  + [recipient] is one exact ParticipantAddress
  + [message_kind] is one MessageKind matching the typed payload variant
  + [subject] is non-empty bounded text
  + [frame_digest] is the WorkPacket frame digest
  + [authority_scope] is contained by both commission and work packet where a work packet exists
  + [payload] is CommissionContract, WorkPacket, ProtocolRequest, ProtocolResponse, CandidateArtifact, ReviewDecision, FinalDecision, or EcosystemFault
  + [proof_refs] is a bounded ordered identifier set
  + [expected_response] is optional exact response kind plus deadline tick and stop condition
  + [idempotency_key] is immutable and unique inside the correlation
  + [logical_tick] is deterministic and monotonic
  = must: validate the complete envelope before append
  = must: reject profile, payload-kind, identity, causation, correlation, address, frame, authority, deadline, replay, cycle, or budget faults without partial append

& [MessageTranscript] is the append-only cycle evidence
  + [messages] is accepted envelopes in exact order
  + [seen_message_ids] is the uniqueness index
  + [seen_idempotency_keys] is the replay index
  + [seen_semantic_fingerprints] is the equivalent-state cycle index
  + [serialized_bytes] is the canonical JSON byte total of accepted envelopes
  = must: make append atomic from the caller's perspective
  = must: require every non-root causation_uuid to identify an earlier message in the same correlation
  = must: require the causal predecessor recipient to equal the caused message sender
  = must: require logical ticks to increase
  - never: edit or reorder an accepted message

& [CandidateArtifact] is immutable mock worker output
  + [candidate_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [content_digest] is SHA-256 identity of candidate content supplied by the fixture
  + [summary] is non-empty bounded text
  + [satisfied_criterion_ids] is the worker claim set
  + [proof_refs] is the supporting identifier set
  + [requested_effects] is the exterior effect request set
  = must: preserve requested_effects for Security review
  - never: perform a requested effect inside this slice

& [DeterministicAdapterSet] is the Phase 1 participant seam
  + [MockCodexAdapter] accepts exactly one assignment and one Cantor return
  + [MockCodexAdapter] emits exactly one fixture-owned ProtocolRequest and one CandidateArtifact
  + [CantorParticipantAdapter] accepts exactly one Cantor query and returns one caller-supplied cantor_core ProtocolResponse
  + [adapter_state] is new, assigned, query_returned, candidate_returned, or faulted
  = must: reject wrong recipient, wrong kind, repeated stage, request identity mismatch, or non-success response
  - never: call a live model, Codex process, network, filesystem mutation, or provider

& [DeterministicObserver] is the Phase 1 acceptance governor
  + [honesty_check] requires candidate criterion claims and proof references to match the work packet
  + [security_check] requires requested_effects to be empty and authority to remain bounded
  + [protocol_check] requires a successful verified cantor_core ProtocolResponse
  + [acceptance_check] requires every WorkPacket criterion to be claimed
  + [effect_boundary_check] requires no effect envelope or effect execution
  + [disposition] is accept, revise, yield, stop, or fault
  = must: record every check result and reason
  = must: accept only when all required checks pass
  - never: claim this deterministic review is model-based FacultyProgram execution

& [SupervisedMockCycle] is the only authorized runtime operation
  + [step_1] validates CommissionContract and WorkPacket
  + [step_2] appends root commission and manager assignment
  + [step_3] MockCodexAdapter emits one Cantor query
  + [step_4] CantorParticipantAdapter returns one ProtocolResponse
  + [step_5] MockCodexAdapter emits one CandidateArtifact
  + [step_6] DeterministicObserver emits one ReviewDecision
  + [step_7] manager emits one FinalDecision
  + [step_8] runtime returns immutable CycleOutcome and metrics
  = must: advance one lifecycle stage per accepted message
  = must: return the first typed fault and preserved accepted prefix on failure
  = must: terminate after decision or fault
  - never: recurse, retry automatically, spawn another worker, or execute effects

& [RequirementSet] is traceable
  + [SML-001] is strict serializable machine forms for commission, authority, packet, participants, messages, candidate, review, outcome, and faults
  + [SML-002] is commission and work-packet authority containment
  + [SML-003] is exact addressing, frame, correlation, and causation admission
  + [SML-004] is message, idempotency, and semantic-cycle replay defense
  + [SML-005] is deterministic expiry and message, byte, tick, and depth budgets
  + [SML-006] is one two-step mock Codex adapter and one existing-core Cantor adapter
  + [SML-007] is one deterministic no-effects Observer review
  + [SML-008] is one successful exact transcript from commission through decision
  + [SML-009] is negative proof for every material admission, authority, budget, review, and adapter fault
  + [SML-010] is deterministic JSON and repeated-run equality
  + [SML-011] is no later-phase or exterior authority

& [AcceptanceAndVerification] is the proof gate
  + [unit_proof] is constructors, validation, subset, transcript admission, replay, cycle, budget, and review tests
  + [fixture_proof] is one exact successful transcript with one real cantor_core ProtocolResponse
  + [negative_proof] is wrong recipient, stale frame, broken causation, correlation mismatch, authority expansion, duplicate message, duplicate idempotency, equivalent-state cycle, expiry, message budget, byte budget, depth budget, effect request, missing criterion, missing proof, non-success core response, and adapter stage faults
  + [determinism_proof] is repeated fixture outcome and canonical JSON equality
  + [global_proof] is formatting, lint, debug tests, overflow-checked release tests, offline locked tests, release build, docs, and dependency audit

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the activation record
  + [fold_1_subject] is continued governed work activates the existing runtime formation's first implementation phase
  + [fold_2_boundary] is deterministic mock protocol inside and live or effect-bearing orchestration outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is commission, authority, participant, packet, envelope, transcript, candidate, review, decision, logical tick, budget, and fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is exact addressing, subset authority, causation, correlation, replay, cycle, expiry, budget, effect denial, and immutable transcript
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is a safe Rust cantor_ecosystem library over caller-supplied cantor_core execution
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is wrong identity, stale frame, broken lineage, replay, no-progress cycle, budget violation, hidden effect, rubber-stamp acceptance, and adapter overreach
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is SML-001 through SML-011 with later phases preserved as growth seeds
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_effect_free_deterministic_mock_loop

